|name3 = Li'l Island Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Whale Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Li'l Island Cat''' when obtained from [[Tiny Fins (Deadly)|Li'l Fish Awakens!]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Due to being the Li'l version of a [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cat]], this unit suffers from a severe lack of good basic stats, making him underperform greatly in his field. For this reason, usage of Li'l Fish Cat prior to unlocking his True Form is not recommended.

==='''True Form'''===
Just like other Li'l Cats, Li'l Island gains the stats to become a viable replacement for his [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Normal]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed/Manic]] counterparts in certain [[Restriction Stage]]s. Besides that, there is little reason to use him as his stats are still inferior to the Normal and Manic Islands.

His increased Critical chance can be ignored, as it still isn't high enough to make him a reliable counter to [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies.

==='''Talents'''===
Li'l Island Cat becomes one of very few units with an [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] niche with talents, allowing it to diverge itself from its stronger counterparts and function as a strong frontline attacker against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies. Its stat buffs further allow it to perform this, even allowing it to dish out more DPS than regular [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] at max level. As if this wasn't enough, however, it also gains access to a [[Wave Attack]], increasing its potential damage even more and increasing its usage against large swarms of Aku enemies. The only talent that might not be worth the cost is '''Resist Curse''', as Relics usually don't pair with such enemies and it can't be used when such combinations do appear anyways. However, even with these perks, Li'l Island requires lots of investment in his (+) levels for him to become usable, but once he has similar stats to your regular Island Cat, he can become a nice supplement to your attacking force. Do note that [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] is much more accessible as a Anti-Aku attacker, having [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] and much more range. Its ability to function without (+) levels is especially important as many Aku-centric stages feature the [[Aku Altar's Seal|Aku Altar]], which disables the effect of (+) levels.

==='''Orb'''===
Either a Strong Up orb for Red or Aku, or a Cash Back orb. Single Surge Counter could see some use, but almost nothing else would be useful.

